4.Inside your insta_clone project, open the android/ and ios/ directories and identify one configuration file in each
(for example, AndroidManifest.xml and Info.plist). Briefly write in a comment at the top of each file what its role is in a Flutter app.

1. Android — AndroidManifest.xml
Open:

insta_clone/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml

Add this comment at the very top:

<!--
  AndroidManifest.xml defines the app's Android configuration,
  including app permissions, activities, and other settings.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

2. iOS — Info.plist
Open:

insta_clone/ios/Runner/Info.plist

Add this comment at the top:

<!--
  Info.plist contains the iOS app's configuration and
  metadata, such as app settings and permissions.
-->
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
